e  i am totally down to spice it up and  switch things up a bit  hopefully we'll get new info soon anyway  and we can just show that but until then  i'm curious to see what you all think so  let me know in the comments  at this point there are just so many  unknowns with the game we don't really  have much to go off of at this point  there's really three big pieces of media  or pr  i guess you could say that we have so  far and that is number one the official  faq on the website the trailer itself  as well as a playstation blog post as  die hard fans of the wizarding world i  think it's important we find ways to  keep the hype remain constructive with  our suggestions but to also try our best  to keep  expectations in check i don't want us to  be set up for a situation where we won't  accept anything less than a perfect game  with every single detail we've always  wanted because as much as i love seeing  the ideas you all have  each and every week on all these videos  there's just no way they're gonna be  able to fit all of that into this game  there's  just no way in developing any game there  are compromises that must be made and i  do think most of you out there  realize this now i'm not saying you  shouldn't wish for the moon if you want  to hope for a fully explorable hogwarts  with branching narrative paths  best-in-class gameplay quidditch diagon  alley young double door and a story with  side quests that rival the witcher  then sure go for it i have plenty of  hopes myself heck i made a whole video  about it but at the same time i think we  need to be careful  not to set ourselves up for  disappointment it's important to  remember avalanche is taking on a  massive task trying to please millions  of fans in what is a very ambitious  project for them  i don't think it's a knock on avalanche  for me to say they just don't have much  experience in this genre they do have  plenty of experience working with other  big time franchises like they do with  the disney infinity series but  not specifically open world action rpgs  in order for them to pull this off here  are my five biggest concerns and what i  think they can do to make it a positive  and not a negative number one a poor  story  look we open every video on the channel  here by saying i'm a dad who loves games  and the stories they tell story is  really important to me in games  but even more so than the story within  the game itself the story that we tell  ourselves and the story around  our lives how the game changes us is  equally important but as for hogwarts  legacy any game drawing huge inspiration  from a book series obviously needs to  make the story a top priority  now there's kind of pros and cons with  this here first of all there's an  enormous  amount of source material to pull from  here ultimately though i think the key  to this game's success will be how  capable avalanche is of  balancing their own original material  but also staying true to the canon and  this is just no easy task here if they  go  too much on the side of their own stuff  then long time fans could feel the game  as a disservice to the original works  and if they play it too safe sticking to  what we already know about the wizarding  world then players will say it's  repetitive and not unique  the devs are certainly saying all the  right things so far  in adrian rob's playstation blog post he  said the following  quote i like to say that what we are  giving fans is something familiar  in a way they have never seen that quote  alone  tells me they understand the balancing  act they've been tasked with  in order for hogwarts legacy to have a  strong original story that's steeped in  wizarding lore they'll need  strong supporting characters the  original series had a huge cast of  strong supporting characters that became  just as beloved as harry potter himself  in some cases even more so than harry  it's also crucial for there to be a  strong antagonistic  force and hopefully there's 