d with too many  generic npcs or standard character  models that we see over and over again  the side quests need to be expansive and  hopefully story driven  try and keep the basic fetch quests to a  minimum maybe most importantly of all  hogwarts needs to feel like a fully  fleshed out character all on its own  this is where avalanche can really let  their attention to detail  of the canon shine considering we  already know so much about hogwarts  and yet while harry potter games  attempted it in the past we've never  been able to freely explore  so many of the iconic locations and  secret passages we know from the books  hopefully the castle is just massive and  a place we can truly get lost in  exploring at our leisure  packing a bunch of epic side quests with  moral choices and i think we'll have a  ton  of replay value number four meaningless  choices  speaking of the moral choices we already  know there's going to be a morality  system  in place for hogwarts legacy but these  can be tricky to pull off  having choice in a game certainly isn't  a novel idea like it once was and to  that point  gamers have come to expect much more  than when morality systems first started  becoming a trend they'll need to make  sure our choices  aren't meaningless they'll need to have  choices with both short-term and  long-term repercussions  ultimately we know will likely end up as  light or dark but the paths need to feel  demonstrably different  this too will help with the replay value  number five  invasive microtransactions in 2020  nothing can ruin a game faster than  microtransactions that come off as  invasive or exploitative  of players wb games should absolutely  know all about avoiding this when you  look back at what happened with middle  earth shadow of war this was i think in  2018.  the loot boxes in shadow of war were so  poorly received that the developer  monolith ended up  convincing wb to have them completely  removed from the game  here's a quote from monolith they said  quote in order to fully restore the core  promise of the nemesis system  will be permanently removing gold war  chests and the market from  shadow of war this means the option to  purchase gold with  real world money and the ability to gain  org followers from war chests will be  removed there will be a specific amount  of time given for players to utilize  their unused gold  if players have unused gold by the end  of the time allotted to spend it any  remaining gold will be converted to  in-game  items close quote look to be honest i  actually think they could pull off  special skins or maybe customizable  broom stuff like that  but at the end of the day i'd much  rather they pack all of that into the  main game and maybe go the story dlc  route if they really want to keep  players engaged for even longer  and have that possibility of an  additional revenue stream down the line  i certainly have high hopes for hogwarts  legacy and i know this is a passion  project for the team at  avalanche it's a huge opportunity for  them  to create something truly special as  always thank you guys so much for  watching  i'll talk to you again soon

